            transition: top 0.2s;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .skip-link:focus {
            top: 0;
        }

        /* Header */
        header {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding: 3rem 0;
            text-align: center;
        }

        header h1 {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            color: var(--text-main);
        }

        header p {
            font-size: 1.125rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        /* Main content */
        main {
            padding: 3rem 0;
        }

        .faq-list {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 1rem;
        }

        .example {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 0.75rem;
            overflow: hidden;
            transition: box-shadow 0.2s;
        }

        .example:hover {
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
        }

        .example h2 {
            font-size: 1.125rem;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .example button {
            width: 100%;
            text-align: left;
            padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
            background: none;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            color: var(--text-main);
            font-family: inherit;
            font-size: inherit;
            font-weight: inherit;
        }

        .example button:focus-visible {
            outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring);
            outline-offset: -2px;
        }

        .example .icon {
            width: 20px;
            height: 20px;
            position: relative;
            flex-shrink: 0;
            transition: transform 0.3s;
        }

        .example .icon::before,
        .example .icon::after {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            background-color: var(--text-muted);
            border-radius: 2px;
            transition: transform 0.3s;
        }

        /* Horizontal line */
        .example .icon::before {
            width: 12px;
            height: 2px;
            top: 9px;
            left: 4px;
        }

        /* Vertical line (makes it a plus) */
        .example .icon::after {
            width: 2px;
            height: 12px;
            top: 4px;
            left: 9px;
        }

        .example button[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
            transform: rotate(45deg);
        }

        .example button[aria-expanded="true"] .icon::after {
            transform: scaleY(0);
        }

        .details {
            padding: 0 1.5rem 1.25rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 1rem;
            border-top: 1px solid transparent;
        }

        .example button[aria-expanded="true"] + .details {
            border-top-color: var(--border-color);
            padding-top: 1.25rem;
        }

        /* Footer */
        footer {
            padding: 2rem 0;
            text-align: center;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.875rem;
        }

        /* Media Queries */
        @media (max-width: 640px) {
            header h1 {
                font-size: 2rem;
            }

            .example button {
                padding: 1rem;
            }

            .details {
                padding: 0 1rem 1rem;
            }
        }

        /* Accessibility: Reduced Motion */
        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            * {
                animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
                animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
                transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
                scroll-behavior: auto !important;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>

    <header>
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
            <p>Everything you ever wanted to know about your feline friends.</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main-content">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="faq-list">
                <div class="example">
                    <h2>
                        <button type="button" aria-expanded="true">
                            Why do cats purr?
                            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="details">
                        <p>Cats purr for many reasons, not just when they're happy. While it's often a sign of contentment, they also purr to self-soothe when stressed or in pain. Interestingly, the frequency of a cat's purr (between 25 and 150 Hertz) has been shown to improve bone density and promote healing.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="example">
                    <h2>
                        <button type="button" aria-expanded="true">
                            Why do cats love cardboard boxes?
                            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="details">
                        <p>Boxes offer a sense of security and safety. In the wild, cats are solitary hunters that need a safe place to hide from predators and stalk their prey. A cardboard box provides a confined space where they can't be ambushed from behind or the side. Plus, cardboard is a great insulator!</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="example">
                    <h2>
                        <button type="button" aria-expanded="true">
                            Do cats always land on their feet?
                            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="details">
                        <p>Not always, but they have a "righting reflex" that helps them reorient themselves during a fall. Their flexible spine and lack of a collarbone allow them to twist their bodies mid-air. However, the height of the fall matters—falls from very low or very high distances can still result in injury.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="example">
                    <h2>
                        <button type="button" aria-expanded="true">
                            How do cats communicate with humans?
                            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="details">
                        <p>Cats primarily communicate through body language and scent. Interestingly, adult cats rarely meow at other cats—they developed meowing specifically to communicate with humans. Other cues include slow blinking (a sign of trust), ear positioning, and tail movement.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="example">
                    <h2>
                        <button type="button" aria-expanded="true">
                            Why do cats bring "gifts" like mice to their owners?
                            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="details">
                        <p>This is often a result of their natural hunting instinct. In a colony, mother cats bring dead or injured prey back to their kittens to teach them how to eat or hunt. By bringing you a "gift," your cat might be trying to fulfill its role as a teacher or provider for its "human family."</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <div class="container">
            <p>&copy; 2024 Cat FAQ Page. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            const faqButtons = document.querySelectorAll('.example button[aria-expanded]');

            faqButtons.forEach(button => {
                const panel = button.parentElement.nextElementSibling;

                // Initialize state: collapsed by default
                button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                if (panel) {
                    panel.hidden = true;
                }

                button.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    const isExpanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
                    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !isExpanded);
                    if (panel) {
                        panel.hidden = isExpanded;
                    }
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
